statement:
On x86-64 with the usual System V ABI, where `char` is 1 byte aligned to 1, `int` is 4 aligned to 4, and `double` is 8 aligned to 8:

```c
struct Record {
    char   flag;
    double value;
    int    count;
    char   tag;
};
```

**What does `sizeof(struct Record)` return?**

Work it out rather than guessing. Lay the members out at increasing offsets, give each one the first offset that satisfies its alignment, and then remember what has to be true of the size of the whole thing.
